			<!-- CHAPTER OVERVIEW: PART 1 (Page iv) -->
			<section class="book-page" id="overview-1">
				<div class="page-body-content">
					<div class="page-running-head">
						<span class="chapter-header-label">Decoding the Burn</span>
						<span class="page-count-label">Overview &bull; Parts I - III</span>
					</div>

					<div class="part-break-banner">
						<p class="part-break-title">Chapter Roadmap &bull; Parts I to III</p>
					</div>

					<h2 class="chapter-title">Chapter Summaries</h2>

					<div class="chapter-content">
						<!-- PART I -->
						<div class="overview-part-block">
							<h3 class="overview-part-title">Part I: The Medical Maze</h3>

							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-1">Chapter 1: Falling Between the Cracks</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">When your mouth feels like you swallowed boiling coffee, your dentist looks for cavities, your neurologist checks your brain, and your doctor draws blood that comes back completely normal.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">None of them ever look across the hallway to see how microscopic gaps under your dental work create an acidic leak that constantly shocks your oral nerve endings.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Instead of accepting the lazy label that your pain is an untraceable mystery, we start with simple physical tests you can run at home in two weeks to see if acid is actively feeding your fire.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
									<ol>
										<li>The 4 specialists who pass you around because nobody owns the borderland</li>
										<li>The microscopic blind spot: why clean 2D X-rays miss fluid margin leaks</li>
										<li>The 2-week acid elimination test: proving or ruling out the chemical trigger</li>
									</ol>
								</div>
							</div>

							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-3">Chapter 2: The Expectation</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Nobody is going to hand you a magic single pill that cures burning mouth overnight, because your dental hardware and nerve sensitivity are uniquely yours.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">The moment everything changed for me was when I stopped chasing miracle cures and began treating my mouth like an electrical circuit with measurable inputs and outputs.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">By tracking what moves your pain from an 8 down to a 4, you take back control from the doctors and build your own roadmap to zero.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
									<ol>
										<li>Why there is no one-size-fits-all cure, and why that is actually good news</li>
										<li>The 'Better or Worse' daily ledger that turns panic into actionable data</li>
										<li>Isolating one variable at a time instead of throwing ten changes at the wall</li>
									</ol>
								</div>
							</div>

							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-4">Chapter 3: The Day the Fire Started</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">It starts out of nowhere: your tongue scalds like battery acid, your gums sting, and you look in the mirror expecting blisters, but the tissue looks completely pink and innocent.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Your dentist tells you everything looks textbook perfect, leaving you wondering if you are slowly losing your mind while the pain steadily climbs.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Nerves do not scream unceasingly without an input: the alarm is real, the fire is biological, and something physical is tripping the switch.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
									<ol>
										<li>The sudden scalding onset with completely normal-looking oral tissue</li>
										<li>The psychological toll of hearing 'everything looks healthy' from five doctors</li>
										<li>The first principle rule: biological sensors never trip without a physical cause</li>
									</ol>
								</div>
							</div>

							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-7">Chapter 4: The Medicine Trap</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">When doctors run out of visual explanations, their default answer is to prescribe heavy nerve suppressors like gabapentin, pregabalin, or amitriptyline to mute your brain.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Clinical trials show these drugs offer partial relief to only 20% to 30% of BMS patients, while over 70% drop out due to crushing brain fog, fatigue, or zero pain change.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Muting your brainstem switchboard with pills does nothing to stop the local acid battery burning away inside your gumline.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
									<ol>
										<li>The pharmaceutical trial gauntlet: Gabapentin, TCAs, and sedatives (20-30% partial response)</li>
										<li>Central nervous volume dampening versus fixing the actual peripheral trigger</li>
										<li>Why brain pills cannot fix a physical hardware leak at the tooth margin</li>
									</ol>
								</div>
							</div>

							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-9">Chapter 5: The Supplement Graveyard</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Every BMS patient goes through the cabinet-filling supplement phase, spending small fortunes on alpha-lipoic acid, zinc, iron, and high-dose B-complex vitamins.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Unless lab work shows a genuine clinical deficiency, medical trials show nutritional supplements help fewer than 15% of patients; in my own trial, fifty different bottles did not lower my score by a single point.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">You cannot out-supplement a physical hole in your tooth enamel or a chemical acid leak that is constantly exciting open nerve pipes.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
									<ol>
										<li>The 50+ supplement experiment graveyard: what the science really says (&lt;15% unselected response)</li>
										<li>Spotting true nutritional deficiencies (ferritin, zinc, B12) versus marketing hype</li>
										<li>Why swallowing antioxidants cannot seal exposed microscopic dentin tubules</li>
									</ol>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>

						<!-- PART II -->
						<div class="overview-part-block">
							<h3 class="overview-part-title">Part II: The Elimination Baseline</h3>

							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-11">Chapter 6: The Elimination Baseline</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">In community surveys, over 75% of BMS patients confirm that acidic foods and drinks make their burning substantially worse, followed by hot spices (58%) and SLS toothpaste (52%).</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">The catch that fools everybody is the 48 to 72 hour time lag: the acidic coffee or sourdough bread you have on Monday does not ignite your tongue until Wednesday afternoon.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">By cutting out all acids for two weeks and learning how to calculate your delayed pain curve, you finally break the confusion and see the fire quiet down.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
									<ol>
										<li>The trigger hierarchy: Dietary acids (75%), spices (58%), SLS (52%), starches (46%)</li>
										<li>The 48-72 hour delayed chemical fuse: why Monday's meal burns on Wednesday</li>
										<li>The 3-day on, 3-day off testing protocol to pinpoint your personal time lag</li>
									</ol>
								</div>
							</div>

							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-15">Chapter 7: Rechecking Hardware - The Exposed Tubule Audit</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Your teeth are not solid marble stones: underneath the enamel sits dentin, packed with up to 40,000 microscopic open fluid pipes per square millimeter.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">When gums recede or dental crown cement secretly dissolves underneath, acids and saliva rush straight down those pipes directly into your living dental pulp.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Because crowns block X-rays like lead walls, standard dental checkups miss these leaks; you need specific tactile micro-checks to find the hidden breach.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
									<ol>
										<li>The 40,000 micro-pipes per mm²: how tooth fluid movement triggers burning</li>
										<li>Crown cement washouts: the invisible shadow that 2D X-rays cannot penetrate</li>
										<li>Tactile margin audits: how to spot abfractions, root collars, and microscopic leaks</li>
									</ol>
								</div>
							</div>

							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-18">Chapter 8: The Chemical Ingress</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Once tooth tubules are open, every acidic sip, carbonated drink, or aggressive mouthwash acts like liquid fire rushing down an open pipe.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">The fluid shift inside the tooth physically bends and fires unshielded mechanoreceptors, sending intense alarm signals straight to your trigeminal nerve.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">This explains why the minty, foaming toothpaste you bought to soothe your burning mouth was actually pouring gasoline on the fire.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
									<ol>
										<li>Hydrodynamic fluid flow: how fluid shifts inside teeth generate pain</li>
										<li>How acidic protons (H+) penetrate straight to pulp nerve endings</li>
										<li>Why popular antiseptic mouthwashes and abrasive whitening pastes destroy receded margins</li>
									</ol>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>

						<!-- PART III -->
						<div class="overview-part-block">
							<h3 class="overview-part-title">Part III: The Discipline of Elimination</h3>

							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-22">Chapter 9: Why Elimination Is So Hard</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Cutting out dietary acids sounds simple until you realize that almost every packaged food, restaurant dish, and healthy fruit is saturated with hidden citric acid or vinegar.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Because your pain has a multi-day time lag, you will be tempted to cheat on Tuesday when you feel great, only to suffer an agonizing setback by Friday and blame the wrong food.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Mastering true baseline elimination requires treating your diet like a clean laboratory bench so you can trust your daily numbers.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
									<ol>
										<li>The psychological frustration of eating plain foods in a world of social dining</li>
										<li>Unmasking hidden industrial food acids: citric acid, vinegar, ascorbic acid, and sodas</li>
										<li>The delayed feedback trap: how the time lag tricks you into false conclusions</li>
									</ol>
								</div>
							</div>

							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-25">Chapter 10: The Diabetic Parallel</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">If a diabetic patient ate sugar all day while taking painkillers, their burning feet would continue to degenerate because the chemical assault never stopped.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Burning Mouth Syndrome follows the exact same logic: your oral nerve fibers cannot heal or regenerate while bathed in continuous subgingival acid.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">When you stop the chemical bath at the gumline, you give your peripheral small fibers the calm window they need to rebuild their protective coating.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
									<ol>
										<li>How small sensory nerve fibers get damaged by repeated chemical stress</li>
										<li>The diabetic neuropathy blueprint: removing the metabolic insult so nerves can heal</li>
										<li>The regeneration window: why true remyelination requires weeks of uninterrupted calm</li>
									</ol>
								</div>
							</div>
						</div>
					</div>
				</div>

