							<div class="overview-chapter-row">
								<div class="overview-main">
									<h4 class="overview-item-title"><a href="#page-58">Chapter 20: An Open Letter to Clinicians</a></h4>
									<p class="overview-sentence">To our doctors and dentists: when a patient presents with excruciating burning and pink, spotless oral tissue, 'idiopathic' is a confession of your tools' limits, not the patient's imagination.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">Look beyond macroscopic 2D radiographs, test for sub-micron crown cement washouts, and respect the multi-day chemical latency of bacterial acid fermentation.</p>
									<p class="overview-sentence">When you partner with your patients as investigative peers, you can stop prescribing lifetime sedative painkillers and start offering genuine physical relief.</p>
								</div>
								<div class="overview-subtopics">
									<div class="overview-subtopics-header">Core Subtopics</div>
